<section class="hero" aria-label="Hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <h1 class="hero-h1">Blog</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">Short, practical posts about working accurately: the calculator habits that cost marks, and the ones that save them.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="page-wrap"><div class="home-layout"><div class="calc-section-wrap" style="width:100%;">
  <section class="home-section">
    <div class="tools-grid">
<% posts.forEach(function (b) { %>
      <a class="tool-card" href="/blog/<%= b.slug %>/" style="--tool-color:#0891b2">
        <div class="card-thumb"><img src="/assets/img/posts/<%= b.slug %>-card.webp" alt="<%= b.imgAlt %>" width="560" height="315" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
        <div class="tool-name"><%= b.name %></div>
        <div class="tool-desc"><%= b.blurb %></div>
        <div class="tool-arrow">Read <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right fa-xs"></i></div>
      </a>
<% }); %>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>What This Is For</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/guides/">guides</a> explain how the maths works. These posts are about everything around it: reading the question properly, estimating before trusting a screen, and the handful of calculator behaviours that produce confident wrong answers.</p>
    <p>They are deliberately short. Each one is a single habit worth adopting, not a chapter.</p>
  </section>
</div></div></div>
